From 520c585cddfdb1fdc8360c7d5d41e0d9a44ce66a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:19:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tracker: fix what the static analysis found

- FSUtils: a typo, !(a || b != c) for !(a || b == c), turned off the check
  that refuses to replace a file with a folder (and the other way round)
  when copying or moving -- the folder-merge prompt came instead, and
  "Replace" deleted the file.
- BNavMenu: a link to an invisible folder deleted the resolved Model while
  a BModelOpener still held it.
- TrackerString: the glob '?' and a negated bracket matched the end of the
  string and went on past it; the 101st '*' was stored past its arrays.
- WidgetAttributeText: starting to edit a rating or a checkbox fits the
  value without a pose view, which the truncation asked for its font. The
  helpers measure with the plain font then, as BPoseView does.
- BViewState: a view mode of 0 passed the sanity check, and every pose was
  created and never listed.
- BPoseView: the lists leaked when "Move to Trash" was cancelled, and an
  empty one on every move; scripting's "delete Entry" deleted the entries
  of an owning list, which deleted them again.

Test: HaikuArmQemu's tools/analysis-fixes/afxtest, tracker-glob (also under
the guarded heap), nav-menu-hidden-link (under the guarded heap) and
rating-edit-without-view.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
